    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d86">

                <pb facs="0104" n="92" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg92"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48/5325: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-01-26T20:00:00-05:00">January 26, 1942—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>301. Your 327, January 22, midnight, is under urgent consideration. We hope the
                    Foreign Office will follow your request that no action be taken on this matter
                    until our views have been communicated to it.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d86-f1"/> We
                    would also welcome any comment the Foreign Office may wish to make.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d86-f1" n="9" xml:id="d86-f1-content">
                <p>The Ambassador reported in telegram No. 410, January 28, midnight: “I have again
                    been assured by Eden that Foreign Office will take no action until we have
                    received your reply.” (840.48/5334)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
